WEBVTT

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.070
<i>The Digimon Encyclopedia!</i>

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:15.580
<i>Greymon.</i>

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.160
<i>This Digimon evolves from Agumon.</i>

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.160
LEVEL: CHAMPION

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.750
TYPE: DINOSAUR

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.250
<i>With an armor-like skin covering the head,
Greymon has a combative look!</i>

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.250
SPECIAL MOVE: MEGA FLAME

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:25.960
<i>Now, let's check this out!</i>

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:31.960
<i>Looks like something amazing awaits
this powered-up Greymon today.</i>

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.010
<i>Let's wait and see!</i>

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.510
<i>Which Digimon will it be next time?</i>

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:48.230
<i>Oh Yeah!
tsuyogatte tobinotte kaze ni natte</i>

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:48.230
<i>Oh Yeah!
Be strong, jump on, become the wind</i>

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:54.320
<i>oozora kidou wo koero</i>

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:54.320
<i>Pass the orbit beyond the sky</i>

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:11.090
<i>osaekirenai maenomeri na speed</i>

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:11.090
<i>Can't hold back this rushing speed</i>

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>minareta machi ga diorama ni naru</i>

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>A familiar town turns into a diorama</i>

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:21.310
<i>futoumei na sora tsukinukerunda</i>

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:21.310
<i>Burst through the unclear skies</i>

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:26.480
<i>nayami toka fuman toka futtobashite</i>

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:26.480
<i>Blow away your worries and discontent</i>

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:31.900
<i>manual doori no tabi nanka irane</i>

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:31.900
<i>Who needs a journey that's by the book</i>

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:37.700
<i>mayottemo furuetemo koudo agete</i>

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:37.700
<i>Even if you're lost or trembling,
Raise the altitude</i>

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:42.580
<i>Oh Yeah!
ikigatte shikujitte tachiagatte</i>

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:42.580
<i>Oh Yeah!
Show off, mess up, stand back up</i>

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:47.790
<i>kimi to mitsumeru michi naru chiheisen</i>

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:47.790
<i>The unknown horizon I watch with you</i>

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.670
<i>saa tsuyogatte tobinotte kaze ni natte</i>

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.670
<i>Now, be strong, jump on, become the wind</i>

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:58.470
<i>asu wo terasu taiyou
mejirushi ni shitesa</i>

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:58.470
<i>Use the sun
That lights tomorrow as a guide</i>

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:04.310
<i>tonde ike jiyuu na Glorious World</i>

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:04.310
<i>Fly off to the Glorious World of freedom</i>

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:12.860
<i>The one-on-one battle between Greymon
and revenge-seeking Orgemon.</i>

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:21.040
<i>The fierce but fair battle
met an abrupt end</i>

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:24.200
<i>due to a sudden attack.</i>

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:34.130
<i>What appeared before them was a Digimon
that surpassed Greymon's Champion Stage,</i>

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:35.960
<i>an Ultimate Digimon.</i>

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:45.390
<i>The power of which engulfed the children
in flames of despair.</i>

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.780
THE STEEL-SOLID SUPER EVOLUTION

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:19.010
<i>Everyone, run!</i>

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:24.060
<i>Oh gee, this is no time to be filming,
Koshiro-san!</i>

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:25.300
<i>Orgemon...</i>

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:27.560
<i>Sora, look after Agumon!</i>

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:30.810
<i>Let's retreat! We have no other choice.</i>

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:38.730
You'll be okay, Agumon.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:42.700
You'll be good as new if you just rest...

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:45.070
This is it!

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:48.160
Ultimate Digimon, Metaltyranomon.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:50.830
Koshiro-kun, isn't this...

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:54.380
I transferred the data left behind
in the fortress here.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.170
When did you...

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:59.550
But the data's corrupted,
so it's difficult to analyze...

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:01.840
Wait, all you got was the name?

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:05.760
Well, we now know that Ultimate Digimon
are extremely strong though.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.310
We experienced it ourselves...

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:15.190
<i>Holy Digimon...</i>

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.520
<i>Lies ahead...</i>

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.280
<i>Go straight...</i>

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:32.080
Retreating was the best option
in that situation.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.330
What could we have done in those attacks?

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:39.510
If we die, everything will end.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:42.890
It's a waste we couldn't gain
enough information though.

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:44.840
We didn't fight for the information.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:50.180
Orgemon... said that it was for pride.

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:53.180
That's why Orgemon
challenged us to battle.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:57.980
Friend or foe...
that's not what this is about.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.610
At that time,
Orgemon had a different motive.

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:10.870
I don't like this kind of atmosphere!

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:14.630
Should I... stop them?

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:15.870
Hmm...

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.130
Please?

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:24.630
Isn't there a possibility
that Orgemon's words were a trap?

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.890
Orgemon's eyes weren't lying!

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:32.140
Making friends with who you're fighting?
You're too naive.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:36.020
If you stay this way... you won't survive.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:42.520
No, I swear I'll carry this out.

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:44.780
I'll save the Holy Digimon

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:47.030
and our city!

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:57.620
Taichi...

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.110
Agumon!

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:03.550
Taichi?!

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:05.630
I'm so glad...

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:07.550
Huh?

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:16.810
Piyomon and the others
will be back with food soon.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.310
What about Orgemon?

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:29.990
I wanted to... finish the battle.

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:30.990
Yeah...

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.330
So did I...

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:43.590
We're back!

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:48.090
Something smells yummy!

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:52.930
We have enough for everyone!

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:55.270
Welcome back, I'm glad everyone's safe.

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:59.810
Well, there were Soundbirdmon everywhere,
so it was pretty tough...

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:07.820
It's only a matter of time
before they find this place too...

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:18.250
What are you thinking?

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:23.540
If you're trying to fight them
without a plan, I can't agree.

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:26.470
Our goal is the Holy Digimon...

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:28.510
That's our priority.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:32.640
I know. We don't have much time...

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:36.010
But the enemy's eyes are
all over the forest already.

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:40.560
To move forward, we can't avoid contact
with Metaltyranomon...

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:43.690
Soundbirdmon...

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:46.770
If we're seen by them,
Metaltyranomon will rush over...

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:52.030
My goodness, you two!

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:57.200
Come listen!
Koshiro-san made a great discovery!

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:03.920
This is...

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:06.920
I found it as I was analyzing the data.

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:10.670
It's where we are,
the map of Cloud Continent.

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:14.180
I'll share it
with everyone's Digivices as well.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:21.430
And... I may have solved
some questions you all had.

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:25.180
First, this is the seaside fortress
where we were at.

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:28.240
It looks like there was
frequent communication

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:31.240
taking place from here
to another location.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:36.740
The words Taichi-san read was also
a part of that communication log.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:40.370
As a possibility,
one of these points may be...

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:44.830
Their headquarters...
where the Holy Digimon is located.

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:46.880
Yes.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:50.460
Which means we should
head for one of these locations.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:54.220
There's also another reason
that supports this.

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:57.470
This is the direction
Orgemon pointed towards.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:00.600
If we overlap that with the map...

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:04.230
Straight...

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:06.980
Straight...

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:10.610
This means...

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:14.990
Orgemon told us
where the headquarters is located.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:17.080
Yes, exactly.

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:19.240
You're wonderful, Koshiro-san!

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:21.160
Isn't he brilliant?

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.580
Koshiro!

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:26.420
Well...

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:30.460
at least this information
sounds trustworthy.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:32.090
Agumon!

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:33.300
Taichi!

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:36.800
And Taichi-san, here.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:05.580
Baby Flame!

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:17.720
<i>This is Taichi,
the diversion plan is working.</i>

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:19.680
<i>Everyone, this is your chance.</i>

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:23.180
<i>Once Agumon and I shake them off,
we'll catch up!</i>

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.620
Is this far enough?

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:45.540
Yeah!

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:48.540
Thanks, Yamato.

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:56.930
Agumon!

00:10:56.930 --> 00:10:58.220
Yeah!

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:21.240
Agumon Evolution!

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:35.420
Greymon!

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:42.130
Here we go!

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:43.470
Yeah!

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:03.530
Mega Flame!

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:08.660
Let's get in real close!

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:09.540
Yeah!

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:15.540
Metaltyranomon, I won't lose this time!

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:54.250
We have to cross this?

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.000
So this is the "straight route"...

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:01.380
Not only is it eerie, but it...

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:03.590
Feels very evil...

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:09.570
Go through a place like this?
Uh-uh, I don't think so!

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:11.600
Ugh, it looks bad for my skin...

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.350
This dark mist...

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:18.400
Or should it be called a miasma?

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:20.520
This is...

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:24.490
the same thing
that Metaltyranomon was emitting!

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.620
Then the "straight route" is...

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:31.240
The usual route that they use...
that's what it means!

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:34.630
Oh, hey...

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:35.500
Huh?!

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:39.460
What's this?
Maybe we shouldn't get too close to it...

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:45.260
How about we try throwing something
into it to test it out?

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:47.260
Here... we go!

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:58.300
Even for me,
swimming through this would be a little...

00:13:58.300 --> 00:14:01.020
Wait! Was that my exam prep book?!

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:05.780
The information was correct,

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:09.870
but this is too difficult for us to cross.

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:11.740
Unfortunately.

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:30.430
<i>This is Metaltyranomon's
analyzed battle data.</i>

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:34.690
<i>When Metaltyranomon switches
from the laser to the missiles,</i>

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:37.310
<i>there'll be an opening for an attack.</i>

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:39.900
<i>If you can somehow
take advantage of that...</i>

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:43.190
<i>This is the only plan
that I can think of right now.</i>

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:50.490
Now!

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:51.950
Greymon!

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:53.240
Yeah!

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:55.790
Mega Flame!

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:24.530
Huh?!

00:15:24.530 --> 00:15:25.940
What is it?

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:35.950
Closer! Get closer!

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:54.850
Now!

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:56.310
Yeah!

00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:58.770
This time for sure!

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:10.600
We can't... lose yet...

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:12.910
I swear we won't lose...

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:37.140
Huh?!

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:50.910
What is that?

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:52.530
Something fell!

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:58.200
Taichi-san! Greymon!

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:07.960
Metaltyranomon!

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:12.110
<i>We... won't lose!</i>

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:15.400
<i>We won't ever stop!</i>

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:31.170
Greymon...

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:37.260
Super Evolution!

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:51.900
Metalgreymon!

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:54.940
METALGREYMON

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:59.110
Greymon evolved even further!

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:01.450
Can this be...

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:03.530
An Ultimate Digimon!

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:23.220
Trident Arm!

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:58.010
Go!

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:01.840
Giga Storm!

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:40.710
We did it, Taichi...

00:20:41.050 --> 00:20:42.430
Agumon!

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:44.650
We sure did it!

00:20:44.650 --> 00:20:48.310
I hope Orgemon was watching.

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:50.180
Yeah!

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:56.400
Orgemon's information was correct.

00:20:56.770 --> 00:20:58.780
But the problem is this.

00:20:58.780 --> 00:21:02.450
Metaltyranomon was fine falling in there.

00:21:02.450 --> 00:21:06.950
Only those who possess the dark miasma
can survive in this environment.

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:09.550
Then we can't go any further.

00:21:09.550 --> 00:21:12.080
We'll have to make a detour then.

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:14.540
Even if we wanted to...

00:21:15.330 --> 00:21:19.340
there's not enough information
to tell which way is correct.

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:23.300
Then... how about we split into two teams?

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:25.470
Looks like we have no other choice...

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:26.430
Yamato?

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:27.770
I agree.

00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:32.100
But what if both are no good or dead-ends?

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:36.230
In our current state,
that possibility is out of the question.

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:39.440
Besides, if something happens to one side,

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:41.240
we can avoid being wiped out.

00:21:41.240 --> 00:21:42.110
What?!

00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:45.030
Something?! What do you mean?!

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:47.450
Something means something.

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:50.910
And how should we organize it?

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:52.410
Who, who, and who?

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:54.080
How about we draw names?

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:57.290
Senpai, let me borrow your notebook
real quick to make it!

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:00.630
Uh, wait! What do you mean real quick?!

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:07.380
<i>korogaru youni gamushara ni hashitta</i>

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:07.380
<i>As if rolling out of control,
I ran frantically</i>

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:11.260
<i>nani ga matteru no?</i>

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:11.260
<i>"What's waiting ahead?"</i>

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:17.770
<i>mukaikaze ga oshiete kuretanda</i>

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:17.770
<i>The headwinds told me</i>

00:22:17.900 --> 00:22:21.320
<i>shinjite susume</i>

00:22:17.900 --> 00:22:21.320
<i>"Just believe and move forward"</i>

00:22:21.770 --> 00:22:24.490
<i>yaburete shitta kuyashisa wa tane</i>

00:22:21.770 --> 00:22:24.490
<i>The bitter taste of defeat is a seed</i>

00:22:24.610 --> 00:22:27.110
<i>It will eventually sprout
And become your wings</i>

00:22:24.610 --> 00:22:27.110
<i>yagate mebuki hane to naru</i>

00:22:27.240 --> 00:22:30.950
<i>I knock on those doors</i>

00:22:27.240 --> 00:22:30.950
<i>sono tobira tataku riyuu</i>

00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:36.790
<i>Because the present shapes the future</i>

00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:36.790
<i>ima ga mirai wo tsukuru kara</i>

00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:39.080
<i>If you want to find a rainbow</i>

00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:39.080
<i>niji wo mitsuketai nara</i>

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:42.250
<i>You must lift your face</i>

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:42.250
<i>kao wo agenakuchatte</i>

00:22:42.380 --> 00:22:47.510
<i>The hands that reached out to us
Make us much stronger</i>

00:22:42.380 --> 00:22:47.510
<i>sashidasareta te ga
bokura wo zutto tsuyoku suru</i>

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:49.590
<i>If you want to catch your dreams</i>

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:49.590
<i>yume wo tsukamitai nara</i>

00:22:49.760 --> 00:22:52.890
<i>Though the step forward is unsteady</i>

00:22:49.760 --> 00:22:52.890
<i>furueru sono ippo mae ni</i>

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:55.640
<i>Try and take it</i>

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:55.640
<i>fumi dashite goran yo</i>

00:22:55.770 --> 00:23:00.650
<i>Because you can surely fly now</i>

00:22:55.770 --> 00:23:00.650
<i>ima nara kitto sora mo toberu kara</i>

00:23:02.270 --> 00:23:05.950
<i>When Yamato risks his life
for Sora and the others,</i>

00:23:05.950 --> 00:23:08.030
<i>a miraculous evolution occurs!</i>

00:23:08.030 --> 00:23:11.950
<i>Next time on Digimon Adventure:
"The Wolf Standing Atop the Desert"</i>

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:14.910
<i>The adventure continues to a new world.</i>
